  "question": {
    "text": "Let&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>c</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>d</mi></math> are in a geometric progression&nbsp;such that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>112</mn></math> and <math><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>48</mn><mo>.</mo></math> If the geometric progression&nbsp;is continued with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi></math> as the first term, then the sum of the first six terms is"
  },
